ric.shift_coverage_error', 'manifest_path': 'work/results/r02/codex/20261117_111421/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json', 'results_tree_sha256':\nSTRATEGY KEYS dict_keys(['status', 'selected_prompt_family', 'recommended_title', 'central_question', 'central_thesis', 'narrative_rationale', 'prior_paper_story_status', 'edit_framing_decision', 'staged_input_impact', 'method_groups', 'results_focus', 'figure_plan', 'figure_specs', 'supplementary_plan', 'forbidden_headings', 'forbidden_phrases', 'notes_for_writer', 'failure_reason'])\n[\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"composition_reliability_overview\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Make the prediction target, training/calibration separation, scale-selection mechanism, and distinct reliability/efficiency estimands legible at a glance.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n    \"group_by\": \"scientific_stage_not_search_order\",\n    \"metric\": \"observed-composition membership and uniform-simplex reference mass\",\n    \"split_by\": \"training-only fitting, independent calibration, evaluation\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 0.98,\n    \"target_height_inches\": 1.6,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"The ICLR text column is the full 5.5-inch text width. A three-part horizontal overview at about 5.39 inches wide and 1.6 inches high allows short labels at 9\\u201310 pt; do not shrink a crowded diagram. Place on page 1 if naturally possible, otherwise page 2, with about 0.30\\u20130.35 page including caption.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 3,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 3,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 6,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 2,\n    \"content\": \"Training X,Y -> fixed ILR center/base scale -> local-moment correction and nested pseudo-calibration selection; separate calibration Y -> finite-rank threshold -> region for an observed composition; evaluator -> coverage and uniform-simplex probe mass across IID/shift. Put all pseudo-calibration inside the training partition. Use no invented region shapes, numerical measurements, model architectures, or causal arrows from surrogate optimization to empirical gains.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n    ],\n    \"source_paths\": [\n      \"results/ideas/03_training_only_conformal_rank_scale_selection/program_1/src/program.py\",\n      \"task/evaluate_final.py\"\n    ],\n    \"outputs\": \"Preserve editable draw.io source and prompt log. Prefer vector PDF exported from that source when available; otherwise regenerate the overview raster at least 2400 px wide. Never enlarge an existing raster. The later writing/orchestration stage owns generation.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"coverage_by_regime\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Expose near-target IID behavior and the shifted Dirichlet coverage deficit without hiding nominal-level dependence in an aggregate error.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"calibration_curve\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"nominal_coverage\",\n    \"metric\": \"mean observed-composition coverage\",\n    \"split_by\": \"K=3 and K=8\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 0.98,\n    \"target_height_inches\": 2.45,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"Two panels side by side within the single 5.5-inch ICLR column give roughly 2.5-inch plotting widths. Three target values and three regime curves remain readable with shared axes, 9-pt ticks, a common legend, and a thin identity reference; budget about 0.40\\u20130.45 page with caption. Use the observed data range, explicitly mark any truncated coverage axis, and do not force a zero origin that erases the IID differences.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 2,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 4,\n    \"content\": \"For the frozen scaled-ILR method only, plot target coverage 0.80, 0.90, 0.95 against empirical coverage for logistic-normal IID, Dirichlet IID, and Dirichlet shift. The fourth series budget is reserved for the identity reference. This is a calibration comparison, not a temporal trajectory. Baseline comparisons appear in Figure 3 and the main table.\",\n    \"uncertainty\": \"The writer may derive deterministic 95% seed-block percentile intervals from the eight existing per-seed coverage records, resampling seeds jointly across levels and cases. Such mean-coverage intervals are not already supplied in the stored uncertainty object and must be labeled as a new analysis of existing results. Do not average per-episode Wilson endpoints or treat test rows as eight-seed replicates.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n      \"final.metric.iid_coverage_error\",\n      \"final.metric.shift_coverage_error\"\n    ],\n    \"outputs\": \"Save reproducible plot source, vector figures/coverage_by_regime.pdf, and figures/coverage_by_regime.png at 300 DPI; LaTeX must reference the PDF.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"paired_region_tradeoffs\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Demonstrate condition-dependent utility and region-mass differences, including the shifted counterexamples to uniform dominance.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"paired_dot_whisker\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"response_and_covariate_regime\",\n    \"metric\": \"scaled ILR minus simplex-coordinate L-infinity: utility difference and uniform-simplex mass difference\",\n    \"split_by\": \"K and metric, arranged as a 2-by-2 grid\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 0.98,\n    \"target_height_inches\": 4.2,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"Four compact forest panels need the full single-column text width, not a nominal half-column figure. Rows distinguish dimensions; columns distinguish metrics. Three short regime labels and three target markers fit at 9 pt. Use shared scales within each metric column, a common legend, and zero reference lines; budget about 0.60\\u20130.70 page with caption. If labels collide, shorten labels and increase height within this budget rather than reducing type size.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 4,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"content\": \"Within each panel show logistic-normal IID, Dirichlet IID, and Dirichlet shift, with separate markers for alpha=0.05, 0.10, 0.20. Utility difference above zero favors scaled ILR; mass difference below zero indicates smaller regions. These signs have different meanings and must be stated separately, never collapsed into a single success rate. Show all levels rather than a favorable subset.\",\n    \"uncertainty\": \"Use each case's paired_baselines.simplex_linf records: utility_difference with paired_seed_bootstrap95 and volume_difference with paired_volume_bootstrap95. Intervals are descriptive 95% seed-bootstrap intervals. Available bonferroni54_bootstrap_interval values apply to utility comparisons only and belong in the supplemental multiplicity table, not as volume uncertainty or exact familywise certificates.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n      \"final.metric.baseline_utility_gap\"\n    ],\n    \"outputs\": \"Save reproducible plot source, vector figures/paired_region_tradeoffs.pdf, and figures/paired_region_tradeoffs.png at 300 DPI; LaTeX must reference the PDF.\"\n  }\n]\nREFS\n{\n  \"campaign_results_dir\": \"work/results/r02/codex/20261117_111421/investigation\",\n  \"count\": 25,\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-17T13:07:31.799273+00:00\",\n  \"queries\": [\n    \"Lei G Sell Rinaldo Tibshirani Wasserman Distribution-Free Predictive Inference For Regression\",\n    \"locally adaptive conformal regression normalized residual scores heteroscedasticity\",\n    \"conformal predi