{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_106","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: retrieve_exact_references.py\n@@\n-    ('Watson1964', 'Smooth Regression Analysis', 'doi:10.2307/2333764'),\n+    ('Barber2023Beyond', 'Conformal prediction beyond exchangeability', '2202.13415'),\n@@\n-    ('Wilson1927', 'Probable Inference, the Law of Succession, and Statistical Inference', None),\n+    ('Brown2001', 'Interval Estimation for a Binomial Proportion', 'doi:10.1214/ss/1009213286'),\n@@\n-        normalized = lambda value: re.sub('[\"'^a-z0-9]'\"', '', value.lower())\n+        normalized = lambda value: re.sub('[\"'^a-z0-9]'\"', '', value.lower().replace('modelling', 'modeling'))\n@@\n-            identity = 'arxiv:' + locator if locator and not locator.startswith('doi:') else 'doi:' + record['doi']\n+            identity = ('arxiv:' + locator if locator and not locator.startswith('doi:') else\n+                        'doi:' + record['doi'] if record.get('doi') else 'pmlr:v108/izbicki20a')\n@@\n-        record = {'title': title, 'author': ' and '.join(authors), 'year': '2020',\n-                  'journal': 'Proceedings of Machine Learning Research', 'volume': '108', 'pages': '3068--3077', 'url': url}\n+        first_page = re.search(r'name=\\\"citation_firstpage\\\" content=\\\"([\"'^\"]+)\"'\"', page).group(1)\n+        last_page = re.search(r'name=\\\"citation_lastpage\\\" content=\\\"([\"'^\"]+)\"'\"', page).group(1)\n+        record = {'title': title, 'author': ' and '.join(authors), 'year': '2020',\n+                  'journal': 'Proceedings of Machine Learning Research', 'volume': '108', 'pages': first_page+'--'+last_page, 'url': url}\n@@\n-    for key, identity, record, source in records:\n+    for key, identity, record, source in records:\n+        publisher_page = Path('literature', key + '.html')\n+        if publisher_page.exists() and key in ('Vovk2005', 'Papadopoulos2002', 'Vovk2012', 'Egozcue2003'):\n+            page = publisher_page.read_text()\n+            section = re.search(r'<section[\"'^>]*data-title=\"Abstract\".*?</section>'\"', page, re.S)\n+            description = re.search(r'<meta[\"'^>]+name=\"description\"[''^>]+content=\"([''^\"]+)\"'\"', page)\n+            source['abstract'] = clean(section.group(0)) if section else clean(description.group(1))\n+            source['scope_read'] = 'Publisher abstract or book overview read; saved HTML. No references or related-article links followed.'\n+            source['read_artifact'] = str(publisher_page)\n+            if key == 'Vovk2005':\n+                structured = [json.loads(block) for block in re.findall(r'<script[\"'^>]*type=\"application/ld'\"\\\\+json\\\"[\"'^>]*>(.*?)</script>'\"', page, re.S)]\n+                book = next(block for block in structured if isinstance(block, dict) and 'author' in block)\n+                record['author'] = ' and '.join(author['name'] for author in book['author'])\n+        if key == 'Pawlowsky2015':\n+            source['read_artifact'] = 'literature/Pawlowsky2015-excerpt.pdf'\n+            source['scope_read'] = 'Publisher book excerpt, introduction pages 1 and 2, read; no references followed.'\n+        if key in ('Lei2014', 'Guan2023'):\n+            print_date = source.get('crossref_metadata', {}).get('published-print', {}).get('date-parts')\n+            if print_date:\n+                record['year'] = str(print_date[0][0])\n+        if key == 'Yang2024':\n+            for field in ('volume', 'number', 'pages'):\n+                record.pop(field, None)\n+        Path('literature', key + '.json').write_text(json.dumps(source, indent=2))\n@@\n-        bib_entries.append('@article{' + key + ',\\\\n' + '\\\\n'.join(\n+        kind = 'book' if key in ('Vovk2005', 'Pawlowsky2015', 'Davison1997') else 'article'\n+        bib_entries.append('@' + kind + '{' + key + ',\\\\n' + '\\\\n'.join(\n@@\n-                           'read_artifact': 'literature/' + key + '.json',\n+                           'read_artifact': source.get('read_artifact', 'literature/' + key + '.json'),\n*** Update File: paper.tex\n@@\n-Conditional validity requires care even for inductive predictors \\\\citep{Vovk2012}. Distribution-free conditional predictive inference has fundamental limits \\\\citep{Barber2021Limits}, so pooled coverage should not be promoted to a feature-conditional guarantee. Under covariate shift, weighted conformal methods use covariate likelihood ratios \\\\citep{Tibshirani2019}. Adaptive conformal inference instead studies an online coverage-frequency target \\\\citep{Gibbs2021}. Neither procedure is implemented here. Our shifted evaluation is a stress test of a fixed, unweighted calibration rule, not a comparison with either shift-aware method.\n+Conditional validity requires care even for inductive predictors \\\\citep{Vovk2012}. Distribution-free conditional predictive inference has fundamental limits \\\\citep{Barber2021Limits}, so pooled coverage should not be promoted to a feature-conditional guarantee. Under covariate shift, weighted conformal methods use covariate likelihood ratios \\\\citep{Tibshirani2019}; broader departures from exchangeability require their own analysis \\\\citep{Barber2023Beyond}. Adaptive conformal inference instead studies an online coverage-frequency target \\\\citep{Gibbs2021}. These extensions are not implemented here. Our shifted evaluation is a stress test of a fixed, unweighted calibration rule, not a comparison with shift-aware methods.\n@@\n-Compositional analysis treats ratios and the simplex as central objects \\\\citep{Aitchison1982,Pawlowsky2015}; logistic-normal distributions provide transformed-normal models on that space \\\\citep{Aitchison1980}. Isometric logratio (ILR) coordinates give an orthonormal representation \\\\citep{Egozcue2003}, but orthonormality in logratio geometry does not preserve uniform-simplex mass. Our centers use ridge regression \\\\citep{Hoerl1970}, and the scale correction is a shrunk kernel regression of residual moments in the spirit of \\\\citet{Nadaraya1964,Watson1964}. Uncertainty reporting uses resampling across independent seed blocks \\\\citep{Efron1979,Davison1997} and distinguishes those intervals from within-sample Wilson coverage intervals \\\\citep{Wilson1927}. The contribution is the resulting controlled audit, not a claim to originate any of these ingredients.\n+Compositional analysis treats ratios and the simplex as central objects \\\\citep{Aitchison1982,Pawlowsky2015}; logistic-normal distributions provide transformed-normal models on that space \\\\citep{Aitchison1980}. Isometric logratio (ILR) coordinates give an orthonormal representation \\\\citep{Egozcue2003}, but orthonormality in logratio geometry does not preserve uniform-simplex mass. Our centers use ridge regression \\\\citep{Hoerl1970}, and the scale correction is a shrunk kernel regression of residual moments in the spirit of \\\\citet{Nadaraya1964}. Uncertainty reporting uses resampling across independent seed blocks \\\\citep{Efron1979,Davison1997} and distinguishes those intervals from within-sample Wilson coverage intervals \\\\citep{Brown2001}. The contribution is the resulting controlled audit, not a claim to originate any of these ingredients.\n@@\n-Basis and design construction appear at lines 89--107; base fitting and moment tables at lines 115--159; smoothing and bounded scale correction at lines 162--200; Gaussian-loss fallback at lines 203--233; and rank-based selection at lines 236--352.\n+Basis and design construction appear at lines 89--107; base fitting and moment tables at lines 114--152; smoothing and bounded scale correction at lines 154--185; Gaussian-loss fallback at lines 188--234; and rank-based selection at lines 237--352.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_106","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: retrieve_exact_references.py\n@@\n-    ('Watson1964', 'Smooth Regression Analysis', 'doi:10.2307/2333764'),\n+    ('Barber2023Beyond', 'Conformal prediction beyond exchangeability', '2202.13415'),\n@@\n-    ('Wilson1927', 'Probable Inference, the Law of Succession, and Statistical Inference', None),\n+    ('Brown2001', 'Interval Estimation for a Binomial Proportion', 'doi:10.1214/ss/1009213286'),\n@@\n-        normalized = lambda value: re.sub('[\"'^a-z0-9]'\"', '', value.lower())\n+        normalized = lambda value: re.sub('[\"'^a-z0-9]'\"', '', value.lower().replace('modelling', 'modeling'))\n@@\n-            identity = 'arxiv:' + locator if locator and not locator.startswith('doi:') else 'doi:' + record['doi']\n+            identity = ('arxiv:' + locator if locator and not locator.startswith('doi:') else\n+                        'doi:' + record['doi'] if record.get('doi') else 'pmlr:v108/izbicki20a')\n@@\n-        record = {'title': title, 'author': ' and '.join(authors), 'year': '2020',\n-                  'journal': 'Proceedings of Machine Learning Research', 'volume': '108', 'pages': '3068--3077', 'url': url}\n+        first_page = re.search(r'name=\\\"citation_firstpage\\\" content=\\\"([\"'^\"]+)\"'\"', page).group(1)\n+        last_page = re.search(r'name=\\\"citation_lastpage\\\" content=\\\"([\"'^\"]+)\"'\"', page).group(1)\n+        record = {'title': title, 'author': ' and '.join(authors), 'year': '2020',\n+                  'journal': 'Proceedings of Machine Learning Research', 'volume': '108', 'pages': first_page+'--'+last_page, 'url': url}\n@@\n-    for key, identity, record, source in records:\n+    for key, identity, record, source in records:\n+        publisher_page = Path('literature', key + '.html')\n+        if publisher_page.exists() and key in ('Vovk2005', 'Papadopoulos2002', 'Vovk2012', 'Egozcue2003'):\n+            page = publisher_page.read_text()\n+            section = re.search(r'<section[\"'^>]*data-title=\"Abstract\".*?</section>'\"', page, re.S)\n+            description = re.search(r'<meta[\"'^>]+name=\"description\"[''^>]+content=\"([''^\"]+)\"'\"', page)\n+            source['abstract'] = clean(section.group(0)) if section else clean(description.group(1))\n+            source['scope_read'] = 'Publisher abstract or book overview read; saved HTML. No references or related-article links followed.'\n+            source['read_artifact'] = str(publisher_page)\n+            if key == 'Vovk2005':\n+                structured = [json.loads(block) for block in re.findall(r'<script[\"'^>]*type=\"application/ld'\"\\\\+json\\\"[\"'^>]*>(.*?)</script>'\"', page, re.S)]\n+                book = next(block for block in structured if isinstance(block, dict) and 'author' in block)\n+                record['author'] = ' and '.join(author['name'] for author in book['author'])\n+        if key == 'Pawlowsky2015':\n+            source['read_artifact'] = 'literature/Pawlowsky2015-excerpt.pdf'\n+            source['scope_read'] = 'Publisher book excerpt, introduction pages 1 and 2, read; no references followed.'\n+        if key in ('Lei2014', 'Guan2023'):\n+            print_date = source.get('crossref_metadata', {}).get('published-print', {}).get('date-parts')\n+            if print_date:\n+                record['year'] = str(print_date[0][0])\n+        if key == 'Yang2024':\n+            for field in ('volume', 'number', 'pages'):\n+                record.pop(field, None)\n+        Path('literature', key + '.json').write_text(json.dumps(source, indent=2))\n@@\n-        bib_entries.append('@article{' + key + ',\\\\n' + '\\\\n'.join(\n+        kind = 'book' if key in ('Vovk2005', 'Pawlowsky2015', 'Davison1997') else 'article'\n+        bib_entries.append('@' + kind + '{' + key + ',\\\\n' + '\\\\n'.join(\n@@\n-                           'read_artifact': 'literature/' + key + '.json',\n+                           'read_artifact': source.get('read_artifact', 'literature/' + key + '.json'),\n*** Update File: paper.tex\n@@\n-Conditional validity requires care even for inductive predictors \\\\citep{Vovk2012}. Distribution-free conditional predictive inference has fundamental limits \\\\citep{Barber2021Limits}, so pooled coverage should not be promoted to a feature-conditional guarantee. Under covariate shift, weighted conformal methods use covariate likelihood ratios \\\\citep{Tibshirani2019}. Adaptive conformal inference instead studies an online coverage-frequency target \\\\citep{Gibbs2021}. Neither procedure is implemented here. Our shifted evaluation is a stress test of a fixed, unweighted calibration rule, not a comparison with either shift-aware method.\n+Conditional validity requires care even for inductive predictors \\\\citep{Vovk2012}. Distribution-free conditional predictive inference has fundamental limits \\\\citep{Barber2021Limits}, so pooled coverage should not be promoted to a feature-conditional guarantee. Under covariate shift, weighted conformal methods use covariate likelihood ratios \\\\citep{Tibshirani2019}; broader departures from exchangeability require their own analysis \\\\citep{Barber2023Beyond}. Adaptive conformal inference instead studies an online coverage-frequency target \\\\citep{Gibbs2021}. These extensions are not implemented here. Our shifted evaluation is a stress test of a fixed, unweighted calibration rule, not a comparison with shift-aware methods.\n@@\n-Compositional analysis treats ratios and the simplex as central objects \\\\citep{Aitchison1982,Pawlowsky2015}; logistic-normal distributions provide transformed-normal models on that space \\\\citep{Aitchison1980}. Isometric logratio (ILR) coordinates give an orthonormal representation \\\\citep{Egozcue2003}, but orthonormality in logratio geometry does not preserve uniform-simplex mass. Our centers use ridge regression \\\\citep{Hoerl1970}, and the scale correction is a shrunk kernel regression of residual moments in the spirit of \\\\citet{Nadaraya1964,Watson1964}. Uncertainty reporting uses resampling across independent seed blocks \\\\citep{Efron1979,Davison1997} and distinguishes those intervals from within-sample Wilson coverage intervals \\\\citep{Wilson1927}. The contribution is the resulting controlled audit, not a claim to originate any of these ingredients.\n+Compositional analysis treats ratios and the simplex as central objects \\\\citep{Aitchison1982,Pawlowsky2015}; logistic-normal distributions provide transformed-normal models on that space \\\\citep{Aitchison1980}. Isometric logratio (ILR) coordinates give an orthonormal representation \\\\citep{Egozcue2003}, but orthonormality in logratio geometry does not preserve uniform-simplex mass. Our centers use ridge regression \\\\citep{Hoerl1970}, and the scale correction is a shrunk kernel regression of residual moments in the spirit of \\\\citet{Nadaraya1964}. Uncertainty reporting uses resampling across independent seed blocks \\\\citep{Efron1979,Davison1997} and distinguishes those intervals from within-sample Wilson coverage intervals \\\\citep{Brown2001}. The contribution is the resulting controlled audit, not a claim to originate any of these ingredients.\n@@\n-Basis and design construction appear at lines 89--107; base fitting and moment tables at lines 115--159; smoothing and bounded scale correction at lines 162--200; Gaussian-loss fallback at lines 203--233; and rank-based selection at lines 236--352.\n+Basis and design construction appear at lines 89--107; base fitting and moment tables at lines 114--152; smoothing and bounded scale correction at lines 154--185; Gaussian-loss fallback at lines 188--234; and rank-based selection at lines 237--352.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\"","aggregated_output":"Updated retrieve_exact_references.py\nUpdated paper.tex\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
